.TH SWATCH 1 "2026-07-26" "swatch 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
swatch \- switch the whole desktop to a theme
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B swatch
[\fIcommand\fR] [\fIargs\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Applies a palette to every themed surface on the machine: terminal, editors,
status bar, file manager, browser and wallpaper. A theme is a directory holding
a \fIpalette.toml\fR and a wallpaper, kept under
\fI~/.config/swatch/themes/\fR.
.PP
Swatch writes theme files and one pointer line per surface; it never rewrites a
whole config. Where an app has no theme-file mechanism, swatch replaces only the
block between
.B "# swatch:start"
and
.B "# swatch:end"
markers. A pointer edit that does not match exactly one line is an error, not a
guess.
.PP
Swatch refuses to apply a palette containing the string TODO.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
Show available themes, one per line. Unfinished scaffolds are listed as such.
.TP
.B use \fItheme\fR
Apply a theme to every surface. Surfaces whose app is not set up on this
machine are skipped, not failed.
.TP
.B status [\fItheme\fR]
Run
.B use
with the writes turned off and report which files would change. Defaults to the
first theme.
.TP
.B new \fIname\fR \fIimage\fR
Scaffold a theme directory from a wallpaper: copies the image, samples its
luminance range for the structural roles, seeds the ANSI 16, and marks the
accent TODO. Extraction recovers structure, never identity.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SWATCH_THEMES
Directory holding your themes, one subdirectory each. Defaults to
\fI~/.config/swatch/themes\fR. Point it at a checkout to keep your themes in a
repository of their own.
.SH NOTES
VS Code and Zen only pick up a new theme after the app restarts. Everything
else reloads on its own: sketchybar and borders are reconfigured in place, and
the terminal tools pick up their theme file the next time they run.
.PP
Each macOS Space keeps its own wallpaper, and System Events has no per-Space
API: its "desktop" is a display. Swatch therefore walks the Spaces with
.BR yabai (1),
setting each and restoring focus afterwards. Without yabai it sets the focused
Space only and says so.
.PP
Dynamic wallpapers are HEIC files carrying \fIapple_desktop:solar\fR or
\fI:h24\fR, often named \fI.jpg\fR.
.B swatch new
takes the extension from
.BR sips (1)
and warns that one palette cannot follow a wallpaper that changes all day.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dt (1),
.BR sips (1)
